me strategy on both? :grin:\",\"file\":\"app/javascript/packs/store/engagement-letter-template/index.js\",\"line\":30},{\"author\":\"david\",\"body\":\"no action needed.\\n\\nIsn't more readable if \\n\\n```suggestion:-9+0\\n  return axiosRequest.get('/engagement_letter_templates', { params }).\\n    then(({ data }) =\\u003e {\\n      commit('setEngagementLetterTemplates', data)\\n      return data\\n    }).\\n    catch(error =\\u003e handleError(error)).\\n    finally(() =\\u003e commit('setLoading', false))\\n}\\n```\\n\\nI don't think you need to throw error, since if you subscribe to this action, you can catch it in the component still.\",\"file\":\"app/javascript/packs/store/engagement-letter-template/index.js\",\"line\":77},{\"author\":\"david\",\"body\":\"please try to keep the namespace definitions at the top after imports as most of the store modules, for easier reading by finding it already in the expected spot.\",\"file\":\"app/javascript/packs/store/shared-templates/index.js\",\"line\":14},{\"author\":\"david\",\"body\":\"since we're safe guarding against undefined, should we check also if it is an array?\",\"file\":\"app/javascript/packs/store/shared-templates/mutations.js\",\"line\":11},{\"author\":\"david\",\"body\":\"that's why we don't export default the store and make it two objects, so we can have all the module imports as \\n\\n`import { \\u003cNAMESPACE\\u003e, module } from ...`\",\"file\":\"app/javascript/packs/store/index.js\",\"line\":22},{\"author\":\"david\",\"body\":\"that's why we don't export default the store and make it two objects, so we can have all the module imports as \\n\\n`import { \\u003cNAMESPACE\\u003e, module } from ...`\",\"file\":\"app/javascript/packs/store/index.js\",\"line\":40},{\"author\":\"david\",\"body\":\"grouping order is \\n\\n```\\nvendor\\n\\nlocal\\n\\nnamespaces\\n\\ncomponents\\n```\\n\\nhttps://gitlab.innovationlawlab.org/ILL/lawlabplatform/-/wikis/Code-Guidelines#how-to-group-imports\",\"file\":\"app/jav